/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate30_vp_methylethanolamine -- the vapour pressure of methylethanolamine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  methylethanolamine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je049761y                16 pts  274.9-320.2 K  Kapteina; Slovik; Verevkin; Heintz
      10.1021/je101259r                16 pts  341.8-451.1 K  Klepacova; Huttenhuis; Derks; Versteeg
      10.1021/je400373d                 7 pts  388-431.2 K  Yang; Feng; Cheng; Zhang et al.
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      (none)

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je049761y (16 pts, 274.9-320.2 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je101259r (16 pts,
  341.8-451.1 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 2.6 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 16 points (1.17 to 10.3 %, mean 2.587 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 432.388 K lies INSIDE the measured span 274.9-451.1 K: the held-out verdict is the test there, no further condition.

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 5.008624 - 1878.4613/(T + -62.8829),
  in-sample R2 0.999948 over 16 points, 274.9-320.2 K. HELD OUT: 16
  points, AAD 15.8476 % against the band 2.6 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 438.36 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 15.85 % against the band 2.6 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  methylethanolamine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je049761y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je049761y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je101259r.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je101259r"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  2.6 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 16 points (1.17 to 10.3 %, mean 2.587 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
